# Line endings matter for what the server executes.
#
# A shell script that arrives with CRLF fails on the VPS with
# `/usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory`, and a `.surql` migration
# with CRLF is rejected by SurrealDB's parser. `.env.vps.example` is copied on the
# server, but it is also read by anyone building on Windows, so it is pinned too.
# (The scripts strip stray carriage returns when they load `.env.vps` as well.)

*.sh text eol=lf
.env.vps.example text eol=lf
migrations/*.surql text eol=lf
.forgejo/workflows/*.yml text eol=lf
